==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|annélidé}}, coined by French naturalist [[w:Lamarck|Lamarck]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈænələd/|/ˈænəlɪd/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-annelid.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# Any of various [[worm]]like animals, of the [[phylum]] [[Annelida]], having a [[segment]]ed body; they include the [[earthworm]] and the [[leech]].
#: {{syn|en|ringed worm|segmented worm}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Pete Dunne|title=IN THE NATURAL STATE|magazine=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/1990/04/01/nyregion/in-the-natural-state.html|date=01-04-1990|passage=Incarcerated in earth-filled boxes, the hapless '''annelids''' face execution in the morning. Death by immersion in fishponds, death by cruel hooks.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Kondethimmanahalli H. Chandramouli, Donald Reish, Huoming Zhang, Pei-Yuan Qian & Timothy Ravasi|title=Proteomic Changes Associated with Successive Reproductive Periods in Male Polychaetous ''Neanthes arenaceodentata''|journal=Scientific Reports|doi=10.1038/srep13561|date=2015-09-04|passage=The polychaetous '''annelid''' species complex of ''Neanthes acuminata'' has a widespread distribution, with names depending on geographic location.}}

